  "description": "The synthetic pin held at 20 kW/m until it is steady (the starting temperature field is that steady state, computed on the case's own mesh), then a 10 ms triangular pulse (peak 10 MW/m at 5 ms) on top of the background, then 90 ms more at 20 kW/m. The pulse adds 49.9 kJ/m above the background, about 315 K of adiabatic heating in the fuel interior. The power history is the TOTAL power, so it starts at the operating value. Synthetic heat capacities. Thermal only; the power history is an input, not a result.",
